{
  "_comment": "Shared POSITIVE cases of the scenario detail. tests/integration/test_p036_a_scenario_detail_conformance.py uploads each `scenario` and requires the route to answer `detail` (created_at is the upload time and is compared as null); simulator-ui/v2/src/api/simulatorApi.contract.test.ts requires the decoder to accept every `detail` unchanged. So a backend answer in these shapes that the decoder rejects, or the reverse, fails on the same file. WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER: refusals (the 400 and 409 have their own tests), stored-only inputs, combinations not written here, lexical bounds other than the two spelled in the last case (the 18-fraction-digit payment amount and the 50-digit anchor amount; the scale-8 storability bound and the 12 integer digits are in the first case), exact large integers, timestamps, and a real HTTP transport. Authored by hand, not captured from the backend.",
